{
  "id": "front",
  "title": "The front: what stays in the main chat, and what goes behind",
  "description": "Experiment alwaysFree (docs/experiments/always-free.md): each case is labelled with the lane the main chat should take — talk, look, do-now (one quick visible action), job (a work chat, before any model when it is clear) or amend (a running job's plan, through background) — and checks the lane, how many work chats it started, its own steps and, for clear jobs, how soon the first word came. Run it with the Orchestrator and following the hand-offs, flag off and on: npm run eval -- front --orchestrator --follow --flag alwaysFree. Amend cases say a job first (setup) in the same conversation. Cases hold on any machine; a job's work chat really runs, in the sandbox.",
  "cases": [
